GP!

00:43:11.810 --> 00:43:18.540
GP where are you?

00:46:32.240 --> 00:46:35.790
Betsy, I think we should go in the office.

00:46:38.530 --> 00:46:39.450
Polly, what's up?

00:46:40.330 --> 00:46:43.100
Nothing, I don't think.

00:46:51.250 --> 00:46:52.030
Betsy, wait here.

00:46:52.720 --> 00:46:55.420
I'm going to go find Bill and Ella and then take a ride to the end of the trail.

00:46:56.070 --> 00:46:57.330
I think we should go stay here.

00:46:57.570 --> 00:46:59.530
Well, Betsy, that's the difference between you and me.

00:47:00.030 --> 00:47:01.870
You're content to sit behind, and I'm not.

00:47:02.270 --> 00:47:03.510
I'd like to know what's going on.

00:47:03.740 --> 00:47:04.620
I'll see you in a little while.

00:47:27.250 --> 00:47:28.790
Stacey, don't you ever knock.

00:47:29.320 --> 00:47:29.660
Sorry.

00:47:30.250 --> 00:47:33.590
I don't usually bust in like this, but we need you both up in the office.

00:47:33.830 --> 00:47:34.630
What's the matter?

00:47:35.200 --> 00:47:35.900
I don't know.

00:47:36.490 --> 00:47:39.710
Richie's been missing since the campfire, and T.P. went to find him,

00:47:39.770 --> 00:47:41.950
and then Dave went to find them, and nobody's returned yet.

00:47:42.230 --> 00:47:46.450
So I figured it would be better if we're all available for duty, so to speak.

00:47:46.710 --> 00:47:47.630
How long have they been gone?

00:47:48.280 --> 00:47:49.420
I don't know for sure.

00:47:49.800 --> 00:47:51.240
Too long as far as I'm concerned.

00:47:51.720 --> 00:47:52.500
